    q: "What's the difference between investment-grade and high-yield debt, and why does the line between them matter?",
    a: "It's a rating line: BBB− (Baa3 at Moody's) and above is investment grade; BB+ (Ba1) and below is high yield, also called speculative grade or junk. The line matters because many investors can't hold high-yield debt, or must hold extra capital against it, so crossing the line changes who can buy a company's debt and what it costs.",
