    a: "The zero is most sensitive, then the 8% bond, then the floating-rate loan, which barely moves. Duration rises with maturity and falls as coupons rise, because big coupons return cash sooner. The zero pays everything in year 10, so its duration is its full maturity. The loan's rate resets every few months, so it has almost no rate risk.",
