    q: "Walk me through a recovery analysis for a company's lenders.",
    a: "Estimate what the company is worth in default: stressed EBITDA times a distressed multiple. Subtract administrative and other priority claims to get distributable value. Assume a fully drawn revolver, since companies draw it before failing. Pay each class in order of priority: secured debt from its collateral, then unsecured claims pro rata, then junior claims and equity. Recovery is what each class receives ÷ its claim. Test a range of EBITDA and multiples, since the answer is sensitive to both.",
