    q: "What's an asset-based loan, and how is it different from a cash-flow loan?",
    a: "An asset-based loan (ABL) is sized on collateral, mainly receivables and inventory, rather than on a multiple of EBITDA. The company can borrow up to a borrowing base that moves with those assets. It suits retailers, distributors and manufacturers with lumpy or cyclical earnings but plenty of working capital. It's usually cheaper, with lighter covenants, but closely monitored.",
